    "Category": "Leveling",
    "Description": "### OVERVIEW\nRaise your spear and fight for glory!\n\nAs a Hoplite, your raw combat prowess allows you to weild a twohanded spear and a shield simultaneously, providing both deadly offense and incredible defense.\n\nStrike foes in a flurry of blows with your spear, or toss javelins from afar to bleed them dry.\n\nHoplites build up Combo Points to unleash devastating shield slams and dominate their enemies.\n\n### ROTATION\n2. HOPLITE  (Legendary: Hoplite)  -  MELEE DAMAGE\n----------------------------------------------\nMail, polearm + shield, thrown weapon. Stats: Strength first.\nBattle Stance turns on the Hoplite abilities: Thrust (for Sinister Strike),\nShield Strike (for Shield Slam), Javelin (for Heroic Strike), Flurry of Spears\n(for Siegebreaker). Pet: a Winter Wolf, given with the Legendary (no taming).\n\nIn combat:\n 1. Battle Stance, if missing\n 2. Windfury Weapon on the polearm, if missing\n 3. Call the wolf (create it the first time, revive it if dead)\n 4. Pain Suppression on itself, at critical health\n 5. Shield Bash, to interrupt\n 6. Kick, to interrupt, only when no other enemy stands within 10 yards of the caster\n 7. Intercept, then Heroic Leap, when the target is out of melee range\n 8. Misdirection on the tank\n 9. Hard fights: Bloodlust, Death Wish, Hunger For Blood (once the target bleeds\n    from Impaled), Shattering Throw\n10. Bladestorm, with 3+ enemies close by\n11. Bloodrage, only when it is not already active\n12. Rampage, if missing\n13. Victory Rush\n14. Execute, on a low target\n15. Devastate, when Sunder Armor has less than 4 seconds left\n16. Sweeping Strikes, with 2+ enemies close by\n17. At 5 combo points: Flurry of Spears with 2+ enemies, otherwise Shield Strike\n18. Colossus Smash\n19. Javelin, to keep Impaled on the target\n20. Javelin, whenever it is ready again (Colossus Smash resets it)\n21. Devastate, taking turns with Thrust until Sunder Armor has 5 stacks\n22. Thrust (combo point builder)\n23. Demoralizing Shout, if missing\n24. Windfury Totem, if not down\n\nOut of combat: Battle Stance, Windfury Weapon, the wolf, Blessing of Might on itself,\nBlessing of Kings on the others, Commanding Shout, Trueshot Aura, Aspect of the Beast.",
    "DifficultyRating": "BUILD_DIFFICULTY_RATING_EASY",
